module

public import StacksFrontier.RingTheory.Henselian.Henselization.Defs
public import StacksFrontier.RingTheory.Length.FlatLocalHom

/-!
# Length is unchanged by base change along a henselization

Let `A → B` be a flat local homomorphism of local rings whose maximal ideal is *extended* from
the base, that is `𝔪_A B = 𝔪_B`. Then `B / 𝔪_A B` is the residue field of `B`, so it has length
one over `B`, and the length identity of Stacks 02M1

`length_A(M) * length_B(B / 𝔪_A B) = length_B(B ⊗[A] M)`

collapses to `length_A(M) = length_B(B ⊗[A] M)` for every `A`-module `M`.

The henselization `A → A^h` and the strict henselization `A → A^{sh}` of a local ring are of
this kind: both are flat and local with `𝔪_A A^h = 𝔪_{A^h}`, by
`IsLocalRing.IsHenselization.flat`, `IsLocalRing.IsHenselization.isLocalHom` and
`IsLocalRing.IsHenselization.map_maximalIdeal`. So lengths of modules are unchanged by base
change to a henselization, whatever the residue extension.

## Main results

* `length_baseChange_eq_of_map_maximalIdeal`: the length identity for a flat local
  homomorphism whose maximal ideal is extended from the base.
* `IsLocalRing.IsHenselization.length_baseChange_eq`: lengths are unchanged by base change to a
  henselization of a local ring with respect to any extension of its residue field, in
  particular to a strict henselization.

## Implementation notes

The three universes of `A`, `B` and `M` are independent, as they are in
`length_baseChange_eq_length_mul_length_quotient`; the strict henselization of a local ring
produced by a colimit construction lands one universe above its base, so a statement pinning
the two rings to one universe would not apply to it.

The hypothesis `𝔪_A B = 𝔪_B` is stated as `Ideal.map (algebraMap A B) (maximalIdeal A) =
maximalIdeal B` rather than through `extendedMaximalIdeal`, which is a reducible abbreviation
for the same ideal, so that it matches `IsLocalRing.IsHenselization.map_maximalIdeal` on the
nose.

This is the ring-theoretic half of the proof of Stacks 0EE1, which compares the length of a
quasi-coherent module at a geometric point of an algebraic space with its length on an étale
scheme chart: the comparison map `𝒪_{U, u} → 𝒪_{X, x̄}` of
`AlgebraicGeometry.Space.chartLocalRingToEtaleLocalRing` is a strict henselization, by Stacks
04KF. No declaration here carries `@[stacks 0EE1]`: the geometric half of that proof is Stacks
05VP, the identification `F_{x̄} = (F|_U)_u ⊗_{𝒪_{U, u}} 𝒪_{X, x̄}`, which is
`AlgebraicGeometry.Space.isIso_chartStalkTensorComparison` and is not imported here.

## References

* [Stacks Project, Tag 02M1](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/02M1)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 04GQ](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/04GQ)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 0EE1](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/0EE1)
-/

@[expose] public section

open scoped TensorProduct

/-- **(Length is unchanged by an unramified flat local base change.)** Let `A → B` be a flat
local homomorphism of local rings whose maximal ideal is generated by the image of the maximal
ideal of `A`. Then every `A`-module has the same length over `A` as its base change has over
`B`.

The fibre `B / 𝔪_A B` is the residue field of `B`, hence of length one over `B`, so the factor
it contributes to the identity of Stacks 02M1 is trivial. -/
theorem length_baseChange_eq_of_map_maximalIdeal
    (A B : Type*) [CommRing A] [CommRing B] [IsLocalRing A] [IsLocalRing B] [Algebra A B]
    [IsLocalHom (algebraMap A B)] [Module.Flat A B]
    (hmax : Ideal.map (algebraMap A B) (IsLocalRing.maximalIdeal A) =
      IsLocalRing.maximalIdeal B)
    (M : Type*) [AddCommGroup M] [Module A M] :
    Module.length A M = Module.length B (B ⊗[A] M) := by
  have hquot : Module.length B (B ⧸ extendedMaximalIdeal A B) = 1 := by
    have hext : extendedMaximalIdeal A B = IsLocalRing.maximalIdeal B := hmax
    rw [hext]
    exact Module.length_eq_one_iff.mpr (isSimpleModule_iff_quot_maximal.mpr
      ⟨IsLocalRing.maximalIdeal B, IsLocalRing.maximalIdeal.isMaximal B,
        ⟨LinearEquiv.refl B (B ⧸ IsLocalRing.maximalIdeal B)⟩⟩)
  simpa [hquot] using length_baseChange_eq_length_mul_length_quotient A B M

namespace IsLocalRing.IsHenselization

/-- **(Length is unchanged by base change to a henselization.)** Let `Rh` be a henselization of
a local ring `R` with respect to an extension `κ ⊆ L` of its residue field — so `Rh = R^h` for
`L = κ` and `Rh = R^{sh}` for `L` a separable algebraic closure of `κ`. Then every `R`-module
has the same length over `R` as its base change to `Rh` has over `Rh`.

The structure map is flat and local and `𝔪_R Rh = 𝔪_{Rh}`, so this is
`length_baseChange_eq_of_map_maximalIdeal`. -/
theorem length_baseChange_eq {R : Type*} [CommRing R] [IsLocalRing R]
    (L : Type*) [Field L] [Algebra (ResidueField R) L]
    {Rh : Type*} [CommRing Rh] [IsLocalRing Rh] [Algebra R Rh] [IsHenselization R L Rh]
    (M : Type*) [AddCommGroup M] [Module R M] :
    Module.length R M = Module.length Rh (Rh ⊗[R] M) :=
  have : IsLocalHom (algebraMap R Rh) := isLocalHom (L := L)
  have : Module.Flat R Rh := flat (L := L)
  length_baseChange_eq_of_map_maximalIdeal R Rh (map_maximalIdeal (L := L)) M

end IsLocalRing.IsHenselization

end
